        "problem": "Find the point of intersection of the parabola ${x}^{2}=5(y-3)$ with the $y$-axis.",
        "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =5(y-3) \\\\ (0)^{2} & =5(y-3) \\\\ 0 & =5y-15 \\\\ 5y & =15 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,3).$",
